      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly! To perform a quick variance check, I calculated the mean and variance of the control group scores. The mean is 51.83, and the variance is 132.27, which indicates some variability in the data. There's an outlier (78) that significantly affects the variance. This could affect the p-value, so further analysis is necessary to determine if this represents random fluctuation or a systematic issue. A clean, stable set would ideally show lower variance and lack significant outliers. It's essential to assess if these deviations are within acceptable limits before moving on with the efficacy analysis.",
      "source": "target",
